  "id": "COMPOUND:18812 - PROTEIN:5780",
  "verbalization": "Homaxisterol A2 is consistently shown to have a target relationship with SNU-387, which in turn is a target of multiple compounds, including Gypenoside Xlvi and another complex molecule. These targets are all implicated in the biological pathways that lead to the formation of SQ20B. The evidence suggests that Homaxisterol A2 may act through a shared mechanism that influences the biosynthesis or activity of these target molecules, ultimately leading to the production of SQ20B. The integration of these pathways implies that Homaxisterol A2 may exert its effects by modulating the metabolic or structural pathways that are common among these targets, thereby contributing to the formation of SQ20B. This relationship is supported by the consistent targeting of SNU-387 across different pathways, suggesting a potential role in the broader biochemical network that leads to SQ20B.",
